                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "*** Product received for free. ***\n\nWarlock's Tower is a unique puzzle game with a good sense of humor- I was very surprised at how long it took me to get to 68% complete in the game, somewhere around 6 hours.  And this was with a Twitch audience watching and helping me along too!  I welcome the challenge it presents- and the music is well done!  \n\nThe game developers really did a good job in teaching the game mechanics to players in a fair way before dropping them off the deep end to the challenging stages.  You may find yourself 10 minutes into the game wondering when it will become challenging. Trust me, it will get quite difficult soon enough my friend!\n\nThe twitch chat integration works really well- so long as your audience is up for the challenge.  It works by allowing viewers to provide suggestions which are actual inputs of movement to each square so wwaa = up up left left.  It gets much more complicated later on, but surprisingly some of my viewers were still able to provide complex solutions to puzzles. Pretty interesting to collaborate with an audience in a puzzle game- definitely one of the reasons why I consider Warlocks Tower to be unique.\n\nIf you enjoy challenging puzzles, pixel art style, chiptune music, and have a good sense of humor then you will certainly enjoy Warlock's Tower!\n\n",
